Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:16:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(upf): simple-switch keeps all PDRs of a session in the
 UL/DL lookups

The DL lookup by UE IP held only the last created PDR ("TODO: Dirty fix"),
and Remove PDR (PFCP Session Modification) left removed PDRs in the UL/DL
lookups. With a dynamic QoS flow added and then removed by a PCF-initiated
PDU Session Modification (TS 23.502 4.3.3.2), downlink traffic to the UE was
then matched to the removed PDR and dropped.

- add: (re)insert the PDR in the lookup list, ordered by precedence, replacing
  an entry for the same session and PDR ID (UL and DL)
- Remove PDR: drop that PDR from the UL/DL lookups; erase the entry only when
  the list becomes empty
- lookup lists are replaced, not edited in place

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
